    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37848" root="لغط" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَاغِطٌ</span></b>  [part. n. of 1]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَيْتُهُ قَبْلَ القَطَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اللَّاغِطِ</span> [<i>I came to him before the crying katà</i>],
meaning, <i>early in the morning:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُغَّطٌ</span>. (TA.)
[See also 1.]

